      "q": "Division A can sell every unit outside for $74, with $41 production cost and $6 external selling expense. B can buy an equivalent verified unit outside for $72. Internal trade avoids A’s selling expense but requires a quality check charged to B. Two equally effective checks cost $5 or $1 per unit. With each division able to veto and requiring a strictly positive gain, which control and transfer-price policy creates company value?",
