      "q": "A repair firm finds both weak initial technical skill and rushed work under pay per completed job. A work sample identifies technical skill before hiring. Paying for verified durable repairs instead of job counts nets $13 per repair rather than $6, after callback and verification costs. Removing verification saves $4, but then technicians can hide callbacks. Which design follows from these facts?",
